<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John D. Sloat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1781–1867</span> · Also known as John Drake Sloat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Drake Sloat was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-navy">United States Navy</a> officer who commanded the Pacific Squadron at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican–American War</a>. On 7 July 1846 he landed at Monterey and claimed Alta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, ending the California Republic. He handed command to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-f-stockton">Robert F. Stockton</a> weeks later and eventually retired as a rear admiral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-d-sloat.jpg" alt="John D. Sloat" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edwin A. Sherman (author of The life of the late Rear-Admiral John Drake Sloat of the United States Navy, published 1... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_D._Sloat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
